-- title:
--   Maximality of the occurrence ideal (3, T_ℓ-a_ℓ)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and work with $\mathbb T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {ℓ | ℓ ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell\nmid N$ (the $U_q$ generators are suppressed, the excluded set being exactly the divisors of $N$). Let $a:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ satisfy $a_1=1$, and let $F=$ [`bridgeProduct a`](def/CuspForm_IntegralLattice.html#L22) $=\bigl(\sum_n a_nq^n\bigr)\cdot E_1(\chi_{-3})$ in $\mathbb Z[[q]]$, where $E_1(\chi_{-3})$ is the integral power series `e1Chi3` base-changed to $\mathbb Z$. Assume (hT) that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ all coefficients of $T_\ell^{\mathrm{formal}}F-a_\ell F$ are divisible by $3$, the operator being [`PowerSeries.heckeT ℓ 2`](def/PowerSeries_FormalHeckeOperators.html#L33) $=U_\ell+\ell\, V_\ell$ with $U_\ell$ extracting the coefficients in arithmetic progression $\ell n$ and $V_\ell$ inserting them. Let $M$ be an abelian group with a $\mathbb T$-module structure and let $\mathrm{red}:\mathbb Z[[q]]\to M$ be any function such that $\mathrm{red}(g)=0$ whenever all coefficients of $g$ are divisible by $3$, and conversely $\mathrm{red}(g)=0$ forces $3\mid a_1(g)$; assume further $3\cdot\mathrm{red}(F)=0$ in $M$ and $(T_\ell-a_\ell)\cdot\mathrm{red}(F)=\mathrm{red}\bigl(T_\ell^{\mathrm{formal}}F-a_\ell F\bigr)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$. Then there is a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_1\subset\mathbb T$ containing $3$ and containing $T_\ell-a_\ell$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N$.
--
--   This is the maximalisation step of the weight-one-to-weight-two congruence argument: the ideal generated by $3$ and the differences $T_\ell-a_\ell$ is shown to be proper, hence contained in a maximal ideal of the integral Hecke algebra of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, which is the maximal ideal at which the mod $3$ eigenvalue system $(a_\ell)$ occurs. It is used in the passage from a system of eigenvalues mod $3$ to an actual weight two eigenform congruent to it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isMaximal_three_mem_heckeT_sub_mem.lean

